# The human gate for sudo, shipped by every host in this repository.
#
# 30 minutes, cached per TTY. A second sudo in the same terminal inside the
# window does not prompt; a different TTY does. This is the deliberate soft spot
# of the design — anything running in that TTY inherits root for up to 30
# minutes — and `log_subcmds` is what makes what it ran readable afterwards.
#
# A ticket is keyed on the device *and* the session leader's start time (sudo's
# timestamp.c, start_time_matches), so a process that later reopens the same pts
# number in a new session does not inherit it: only what is already in this
# session does, which is the soft spot above.
#
# The factor behind this gate is the host's own and stays per host: the server
# keeps SSH_AUTH_SOCK for pam_rssh and installs lib/sudoers/11-agent-socket
# beside this file, while the laptop's pam_u2f needs nothing kept. This file is
# the part both must agree on, so neither image carries a copy of it.
Defaults timestamp_timeout=30
Defaults timestamp_type=tty
Defaults log_subcmds
